        "description": "<div id=\"link_wrapped_content\">\n<body><section class=\"wp-block-bigbite-multi-title\"><div class=\"container\"></div></section>\n\n\n\n<p>GeForce Now is a pretty good solution for PC gaming if you\u2019ve got a big game library, but want to access it remotely, or just without high-powered hardware. But the system is, of course, <a href=\"https://www.pcworld.com/article/2791898/nvidia-geforce-now-ad-free-1440p-cloud-gaming-plan-is-40-off.html\">heavily reliant upon Nvidia</a> \u2014 they built the service and the servers, after all. But what if you want to access it without giving Nvidia control of every part of the experience? Say hi to OpenNow, an open source client for GeForce Now.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>That\u2019s pretty much the end of it. <a href=\"https://github.com/OpenCloudGaming/OpenNOW\">According to the project\u2019s GitHub page</a>, it\u2019s a project that \u201caims to give players a transparent, customizable alternative to the official client without hiding the technical parts from contributors.\u201d Notably it\u2019s absolutely n",
